{{Documentation}}
This template is for displaying the [[Cat Guide]] given unit names, levels, and talent upgrade numbers.

==Parameters==
<pre>
{{CatGuide
|unit1|level1|talent1
|unit2|level2|talent2
|unit3|level3|talent3
...
}}
</pre>
These parameters work in the exact same way as [[Template:Nyanko]] as this template directly relies on its module for displaying unit icons. What the parameters are for is listed below. Essentially, this template takes an entire list of these parameters and organizes them into the Cat Guide. The order of units shown in the Cat Guide within each rarity will be the same order used in the template call, but it is fine if the parameters are not sorted by rarity.
*<code>unit</code> is the name of the form you want to show.
*<code>level</code> is the level of the Cat.
**If level is ?, then the icon used is the placeholder deploy icon and level is converted to 0.
*<code>talent</code> is as follows:
**0 - No Talents unlocked/unit doesn't have Talents
**1 - One regular Talent unlocked
**2 - Two regular Talents unlocked
**3 - Three regular Talents unlocked
**4 - Four regular Talents unlocked
**5 - Five regular Talents unlocked
**6 - Full regular Talents unlocked (Certain units have six talents)
**7 - One Ultra Talent unlocked
**8 - Two Ultra Talents unlocked
**9 - Three Ultra Talents unlocked

Another option is to omit all of the levels and talents to only show the unit icons. For this, the format is the following:
<pre>
{{CatGuide
|unit1
|unit2
|unit3
...
}}
</pre>
The <code>unit</code> parameters work the same way.

